DoD 4 — THE TRACE PROBE'S FULL SOURCE (companion to comment-7b83957c). Recreate at `apps/daemon/src/orchestrator/zz-trace-ca28be90.test.ts` and run the command in that comment. Deleted after use, so this is the only record of it.

```ts
import { appendFileSync, mkdtempSync } from "node:fs";
import { tmpdir } from "node:os";
import { join } from "node:path";
import { it } from "vitest";
import { SqliteEventStore } from "@moe/store";
import {
  GOAL_CREATE_COMMAND_ID, PROJECT_ID, GOAL_ID, driveThrough, envelope, send,
} from "../bootstrap/bootstrap-test-fixtures.js";
import { runDesignSubmitEdge } from "../daemon-command-design.js";
import { readDesignRevision } from "../design/design-store.js";
import { designRevisionFixture } from "../design/design-test-fixtures.js";
import { installTestRecoveryBinding } from "../identity/session-test-fixtures.js";
import { PRD, approveGate1, committedRevision } from "../planning/plan-reject-test-fixtures.js";
import { compilerMission } from "./agent-mission-text.js";
import { createDesignBriefResolver } from "./wrapper-mission-inputs.js";

const OUT = process.env["MOE_TRACE_OUT"]!;
const say = (...a: unknown[]): void => { appendFileSync(OUT, `${a.map(String).join(" ")}\n`); };

it("traces the compiler mission a real seat receives on a store with a submitted design", () => {
  const storePath = join(mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "moe-trace-")), "trace.sqlite");
  const store = SqliteEventStore.openForProject(storePath, PROJECT_ID);
  say("STORE PATH   :", storePath);
  say("DURABILITY   :", store.getHealth().durability);

  installTestRecoveryBinding(store);
  driveThrough(store, "goal.create");
  const bound = send(store, envelope("goal.create_with_source", 0, {
    instructions: "Bind a PRD for the design trace.",
    source: { displayPath: "docs/prd.md", mediaType: "text/markdown", text: PRD },
    title: "Design trace goal",
  }, GOAL_CREATE_COMMAND_ID));
  if (!bound.ok) throw new Error(`bind refused: ${bound.code}`);
  const ref = committedRevision(store);
  approveGate1(store, ref);

  const decision = runDesignSubmitEdge({
    envelope: {
      commandId: "trace-design-submit", correlationId: "trace-design", expectedVersion: 0,
      payload: { contractRef: ref, goalRef: GOAL_ID, revision: designRevisionFixture() },
    },
    now: () => "2026-09-07T09:05:00.000Z",
    principalId: "designer-agent", projectId: PROJECT_ID, store,
  });
  say("design.submit:", decision.resultCode, "/", decision.disposition);

  const read = readDesignRevision(store, { goalRef: GOAL_ID, projectId: PROJECT_ID });
  if (!read.ok) throw new Error(read.code);
  say("GOAL REF     :", GOAL_ID);
  say("VERSIONS     :", read.versions.join(","), "| version read:", read.record.version);

  const KIND = "planning.submit_decomposition";
  const brief = createDesignBriefResolver({ projectId: PROJECT_ID, store })(KIND, GOAL_ID);
  say("BRIEF        :", JSON.stringify(brief));
  const text = compilerMission("work-trace", KIND, "2026-09-07T12:00:00.000Z", GOAL_ID,
    null, null, PROJECT_ID, brief);
  say("CONTAINS REF :", text.includes(`${GOAL_ID}@v${String(read.record.version)}`));
  const at = text.indexOf("A DESIGN EXISTS");
  say("EXCERPT      :", text.slice(at, at + 300));
  say("UNWIRED CTRL :", compilerMission("work-trace", KIND, "2026-09-07T12:00:00.000Z", GOAL_ID,
    null, null, PROJECT_ID, null).includes("NO DESIGN ACCOMPANIES"));
  store.close();
});
```

TWO FAILED ATTEMPTS FIRST, recorded so the next agent does not repeat them: (1) a plain `node $TEMP/probe.mjs` cannot resolve `@moe/store` from outside the repo; (2) moved into `apps/daemon`, it then died on `Cannot find module .../identity/session-test-fixtures.js` — production modules in this tree carry `.js` bridge files but TEST FIXTURE modules do not, so only a bundler-resolved runner (vitest) can load them. `store.health()` does not exist either; the accessor is `getHealth()`.

The DURABLE equivalent of this trace is committed: `wrapper-mission-inputs.test.ts` drives the same resolver against a real store on every run. The probe adds only what a committed unit arm does not — the real `design.submit` command edge and a WAL_FILE on-disk store.
